{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1503831-rite-of-sanctification","id":1503831,"title":"Rite of sanctification","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-24T11:50:15-08:00","id":1503831,"title":"Rite of sanctification","content":"Alright so one of my player is starting to get really interested in this and is planning to develop plants knowledge to be able to make talens and plant-based preparations. While there are a few examples in somes books, like in the Storyteller handbook p62, I was wondering if anyone had already used extensively the Rite of awakening in its Sanctification version ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T15:40:57-08:00","id":1503850,"title":"","content":"This is definitely one area where there should have been more support as this is a low level rite, and one we can expect lots of PCs would want to use.<br /> <br /> The first Players Handbook has a list of some sanctified plants and their benefits, and I believe the first Wendigo Tribebook has examples of plants that are supposed to be &quot;always&quot; sanctified even without the rite. There is also a mention in Valkenburg Foundation that sanctified wolfsbane requires a Garou to make a Willpower against the talen's Gnosis of 6. When Axis Mundi describes plant spirits like Ayahuasca and other entheogens, it mentions that sanctified versions might provide benefits like the Gift: Sight From Beyond. There are various easter eggs like this spread all over the place, but they are frustrating to collect.<br /> <br /> What I suggest is that you start first with the benefits you want to provide, and then match various plants to them rather than start with the plants and then try to come up with something. I would also have multiple plants be able to provide the same benefit for at least some things. It's redundant, but it also prevents players having to get that one plant, and that only one plant, that can product whatever effect you need. It also reduces the complexity of what you need to keep track of as an ST. Ideally, you want to limit your notes on this to one page. Make it easy for yourself - and your players.<br /> <br /> I would group plants into categories with similar benefits using the canonical examples as a guide. Examples of what I would use would include:<br /> <br /> Plants that Protect Against Magic (they provide a +2 difficulty to the use of supernatural powers per type of creature (Faerie Arts, Vampire Disciplines, Demonic Powers, etc.)<br /> <br /> Plants that Drive Away Supernatural Creatures (they must make a Willpower roll against the plants Gnosis; Wolfsbane for Garou, Garlic for Vampires, etc.)<br /> <br /> Plants that Lower the Difficulties for Certain Rites (Rite of Summoning, Rite of Cleansing, Rite of Contrition, a Seasonal Rite, etc.)<br /> <br /> Plants that Provide the Benefits of single use Gifts (Resist Toxin, Sight from Beyond, etc.)<br /> <br /> Come up with individual powers per group that you feel comfortable with, and then try to match certain plants to those<br /> <br /> Plants that cure Aggravated Wounds by type of injury (like the examples of Burdock and Lodgepole Pine in the Players Guide)<br /> <br /> Plants that Aid in Alleviating Illness (-2 difficulty to Medicine rolls for various illnesses based on the plant itself; other examples in the Players Guide)<br /> <br /> When it comes to healing, this is an area where I think it is often more flavor text than something useful to PCs. So to expedite things, I'll allow them to do things like maintain an herbal garden with a variety of generic plants, and then just have them roll Occult or Medicine to determine which herb they need and then they can make their medicine roll. That way they can serve in the role of folk doctor whose folk remedies can help people get through sore throats, bad fevers, stomache pain, etc. Them using chamomile, cinquefoil, fennel, valerian, etc, just becomes flavor text.<br /> <br /> But if they want something that reduces difficulties or provide other real benefits to things that have an impact on game, then I have them collect individual plants. That's when they need to know they specifically need garlic, hawthorn, mistletoe, henbane, tobacco, etc. to produce the benefit they want. <br /> <br /> I would also make these sanctified plants to be good only for a certain amount of time after harvesting so they just can't keep stockpiling benefits indefinitely. It's one thing to get that bonus one time because they specifically prepared for it, and for them to always have the bonus because they have a spice cabinet filled with stuff they harvested in downtime. Personally I would want scenes more like Aragorn asking Sam to find kingsfoil rather than having a Theurge pull out a spice rack from his Magpie's Swag and always having access to some powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0d0ZslGu6x8\" data-code=\"0d0ZslGu6x8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0d0ZslGu6x8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> You probably also want to note whether the plant can be found natively in the wild in the place you set your chronicle, or if it requires special cultivation to get access (like growing it yourself outdoors, needing a greenhouse, needing the plant to be in bloom or at a special time of year, if it is only found in certain geographical locations, needing to travel elsewhere by Moonbridge or Moonpath, etc.). The ease of getting it is really something that should be decided between you and the player. Everyone will have a different opinion You may want some plants to be easily obtained and sanctified, and others to be more difficulty because of their potency, rarity, etc.<br /> <br /> Rather than put all the burden on you as ST to do this, I recommend putting a lot of the onus on the player who is interested in this and the the two of you collaborate. Let him do the research on the folklore of plants, folk medicines, etc. to come up with a list of plants and their supposed properties, and then the two of you can decide where to slot it and the specific power. There are library books and online resources that can provide a lot of help for this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T01:57:20-08:00","id":1504184,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for you answer, this will help me a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}